    <title><![CDATA[GenMetaFilter支援中繼資料語意解析 避免代碼誤判致文檔搜尋錯誤]]></title>
    <link>https://github.com/infiniflow/ragflow/releases/tag/dev-20261125</link>
    <itunes:title><![CDATA[GenMetaFilter支援中繼資料語意解析 避免代碼誤判致文檔搜尋錯誤]]></itunes:title>
    <itunes:author><![CDATA[martincivan]]></itunes:author>
    <itunes:summary>
      <![CDATA[<h3>Summary</h3>
<p><code>GenMetaFilter</code> is handed the bare metadata value lists. When the values<br>
are codes (<code>SP</code>, <code>DRP</code>, <code>F3</code>), the model can see which values exist but<br>
not what any of them means. A question phrased in words then has nothing<br>
to match against. The model picks a plausible-looking code, and because<br>
the conditions become a hard document scope, a wrong pick quietly<br>
searches the wrong subset of documents.</p>
<p>Co-authored-by: Martin Civáň <a href="mailto:martin.civan@nases.gov.sk">martin.civan@nases.gov.sk</a></p>]]>
    </itunes:summary>
